**Pareto front assessment:**

The tension is clear: high modulus tends to come with low pore fraction (long wait times, cold bath, high polymer), while high pore fraction tends to come with lower modulus.

The most interesting region is **moderate-to-high modulus with high pore fraction**. The condition `17-0add-12deg-150s-N2-1800s` (bath_temp=12, wait=150s, speed=15) gave modulus=267 and PF=0.601 with good quality (full coverage, minor wrinkle only). The condition `17-0add-16deg-120s-N2-1800s_run4` gave modulus=254, PF=0.681 with 2 discards.

Run2 of bath_temp=16 gave 302.6 modulus and 0.763 PF — but had 2 bp1 misplacements and only 2 surviving specimens (SD=0 on most metrics), making it unreliable. Run3 gave 277/0.420, run4 gave 254/0.681. The variability across runs at bath_temp=16 is very high.

**The 17-0add-12deg-150s-N2-1800s** condition (single run) showed promising balanced performance: modulus=267, PF=0.600, good quality membrane, no discards. This is a strong Pareto candidate that has not been independently validated.

This condition warrants a validation repeat before treating it as confirmed.

