**Pareto front assessment:**
- High-modulus region (~350-440 bar): pore fractions ~0.32-0.39 — low PF
- High-PF region (~0.60-0.76): moduli ~225-302 bar — moderate modulus
- The **17-0add-12deg-150s-N2-1800s** condition (run1) shows modulus=267, PF=0.601 with good quality. Run2 shows 382/0.320 — very different, high variability between runs.
- **17-0add-16deg-120s-N2-1800s_run4**: modulus=254, PF=0.681 — but run2 had 302/0.763 (high discard, misplaced bp1), run3 had 277/0.420. High run-to-run variability.

**The most promising balanced candidate on the Pareto front** is the **bath_temp=12°C, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=150s** condition (17-0add-12deg-150s-N2-1800s), which across 4 runs shows:
