- Run4: 297/0.427 (top/bottom gap defect)

The runs show high variability and inconsistent quality. The condition hasn't been confirmed as reproducibly good.

**The 17-0add-16deg-120s-N2-1800s** condition also shows promise but with similarly high variability.

**Better-validated candidates:** The **17-0add-22deg-200s-N2-1450s** condition has 11 runs with mean modulus ~250 bar and mean PF ~0.52 — well-validated but not on the Pareto front for high modulus.

**Unexplored region:** Combining moderate bath temperature (~12-16°C) with slightly longer wait times or different pullcast speeds to push toward higher modulus while maintaining PF > 0.5. The data suggests bath_temp around 12-16°C with N2 and polymer_wt=17 gives moderate-to-high modulus. The 17-0add-15deg-30s-N2-1200s condition (7 runs) shows mean modulus ~277 bar and mean PF ~0.47 — reasonable but not Pareto-dominant.

**Decision:** The 17-0add-12deg-150s-N2-1800s condition is a Pareto-front candidate (run1 showed 267/0.601) but has not been reproduced reliably — 3 of 4 runs had coverage defects and divergent measurements. However, run1 had good quality. I should explore a nearby condition that might improve both objectives. 

